IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa20-part26`

-- coa20-part26a.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 26A (Arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty),
-- ss 901A to 901L, lines 12332-12527 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. LAYER 1, objective. Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (see coa20-part26.l4 for how to read them).
-- Sections 901D, 901E, 901H, 901J and 901K are the twins of ss 897, 898, 899A, 900 and 901: they are instantiated from the twin's
-- block by work/expand.py (renaming and re-pointing the quotations), and the differences that matter are written by hand
-- beside them: 901D(7)-(8) (the penalty is split by country), 901K(2) (a second condition). The "Part 26 has no headcount test,
-- Part 26A has none" difference is in 901F(1) and 901G(5). Names and quotations are checked by srcrefs.py.

-- A requirement to be applied to an applicant list, instantiated twice below (ss 901C(2) and 901F(3)).

-- ===========================================================================================================
§ `Part 26A -- Arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty`
-- ===========================================================================================================

§§ `Application of this Part (s 901A)`

-- JURAL none (a rule fixing the scope of the Part)
-- src:12335 | (1) The provisions of this Part apply where conditions A and B are met in relation to a company.
@ref s 901A(1) The Part applies where conditions A and B are met (src:12335)
GIVEN `condition A is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition B is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901A(1) the provisions of Part 26A apply` MEANS
    IF `condition A is met` AND `condition B is met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this Part apply where conditions A and B are met in relation to a company"

-- "financial difficulties that are affecting, or will or may affect, its ability to carry on business as a going concern" is an
-- open-textured judgment: it is taken as a plain input, never guessed.
-- src:12336 | (2) Condition A is that the company has encountered, or is likely to encounter, financial difficulties that are affecting, or will or may affect, its ability to carry on business as a going concern.
@ref s 901A(2) Condition A: financial difficulties affecting the ability to carry on business as a going concern (src:12336)
GIVEN `the company has encountered financial difficulties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is likely to encounter financial difficulties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those difficulties are affecting, or will or may affect, its ability to carry on business as a going concern` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901A(2) condition A is met` MEANS
    IF (`the company has encountered financial difficulties` OR `the company is likely to encounter financial difficulties`)
       AND `those difficulties are affecting, or will or may affect, its ability to carry on business as a going concern`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition A is that the company has encountered, or is likely to encounter, financial difficulties that are affecting, or will or may affect, its ability to carry on business as a going concern"

-- src:12337 | (3) Condition B is that—
-- src:12338 | (a) a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and—
-- src:12339 | (i) its creditors, or any class of them, or
-- src:12340 | (ii) its members, or any class of them, and
-- src:12341 | (b) the purpose of the compromise or arrangement is to eliminate, reduce or prevent, or mitigate the effect of, any of the financial difficulties mentioned in subsection (2).
@ref s 901A(3) Condition B: a compromise or arrangement proposed to deal with the financial difficulties (src:12337-12341)
GIVEN `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its creditors, or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its members, or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the compromise or arrangement is to eliminate, reduce or prevent, or mitigate the effect of, any of the financial difficulties mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901A(3) condition B is met` MEANS
    IF (`a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its creditors, or any class of them` OR `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its members, or any class of them`)
       AND `the purpose of the compromise or arrangement is to eliminate, reduce or prevent, or mitigate the effect of, any of the financial difficulties mentioned in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition B is that— (a) a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and ..., and (b) the purpose of the compromise or arrangement is to eliminate, reduce or prevent, or mitigate the effect of, any of the financial difficulties"

-- JURAL none (a definition)
-- src:12342 | (4) In this Part—
-- src:12343 | “arrangement” includes a reorganisation of the company’s share capital by the consolidation of shares of different classes or by the division of shares into shares of different classes, or by both of those methods;
@ref s 901A(4) "arrangement" includes a reorganisation of the share capital (src:12342-12343)
GIVEN `by the consolidation of shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by the division of shares into shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901A(4) the reorganisation of the share capital is an arrangement` MEANS
    IF `by the consolidation of shares of different classes` OR `by the division of shares into shares of different classes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“arrangement” includes a reorganisation of the company’s share capital by the consolidation of shares of different classes or by the division of shares into shares of different classes, or by both"

DECLARE `s 901A(4) place where the word company is used` IS ONE OF
    `s 901A(4) in section 901J`
    `s 901A(4) elsewhere in Part 26A`

-- JURAL none (a definition)
-- src:12344 | “company”—
-- src:12345 | (a) in section 901J (powers of court to facilitate reconstruction or amalgamation) means a company within the meaning of this Act, and
-- src:12346 | (b) elsewhere in this Part means any company liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 901A(4) "company" in s 901J and elsewhere in Part 26A (src:12344-12346)
GIVEN place IS A `s 901A(4) place where the word company is used`
      `s 1(1) the body is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901A(4) the body is a company for the purposes of Part 26A` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 901A(4) in section 901J` THEN `s 1(1) the body is a company` -- "means a company within the meaning of this Act": the seam answer
    WHEN `s 901A(4) elsewhere in Part 26A` THEN `the body is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` -- "means any company liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 ...": a borrowed definition, an input (NOTHING = not known)

-- JURAL none (a rule of precedence between Parts)
-- src:12347 | (5) The provisions of this Part have effect subject to Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) where that Part applies (see sections 902 and 903).
@ref s 901A(5) Part 26A has effect subject to Part 27 where that Part applies (src:12347)
GIVEN `s 902(1) this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901A(5) the provisions of Part 26A have effect subject to Part 27` MEANS
    IF `s 902(1) this Part applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) where that Part applies"

§§ `Power to exclude companies providing financial services, etc (s 901B)`

-- The power to make the regulations is machinery (inert, reason 2, see the coverage row). What the regulations DO is a plain input:
-- JURAL the company or creditors the regulations name: immunity from Part 26A | whoever proposes the compromise or arrangement: disability
-- src:12349 | (1) The Secretary of State may by regulations provide that this Part does not apply—
-- src:12350 | (a) where the company in respect of which a compromise or arrangement is proposed is an authorised person, or an authorised person of a specified description;
-- src:12351 | (b) where—
-- src:12352 | (i) a compromise or arrangement is proposed between a company, or a company of a specified description, and any creditors of the company, and
-- src:12353 | (ii) those creditors consist of or include creditors of a specified description.
@ref s 901B(1) Regulations may provide that Part 26A does not apply (src:12349-12353)
GIVEN `regulations under section 901B provide that Part 26A does not apply to the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901B(1) Part 26A does not apply because of regulations under section 901B` MEANS
    IF `regulations under section 901B provide that Part 26A does not apply to the compromise or arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations, if any, are not among the sources; without them the section says nothing

-- src:12354 | (2) In this section—
-- src:12355 | “authorised person” has the same meaning as in the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 31 of that Act);
-- src:12356 | “specified” means specified in the regulations.
@ref s 901B(2) "authorised person" and "specified" (src:12354-12356)
GIVEN `the person has the meaning of authorised person given by section 31 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901B(2) the person is an authorised person` MEANS
    `the person has the meaning of authorised person given by section 31 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the same meaning as in the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 31 of that Act)"; the borrowed answer is supplied

GIVEN `the description is specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901B(2) the description is specified` MEANS
    IF `the description is specified in the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified” means specified in the regulations"

-- src:12357 | (3) Regulations under this section are subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
-- s 901B(3): regulations under this section are subject to affirmative resolution procedure: machinery (inert, reason 2). No L4.

§§ `Court order for holding of meeting (s 901C)`

-- JURAL the creditors or members concerned: liability to be summoned | the court: power
-- src:12360 | (1) The court may, on an application under this subsection, order a meeting of the creditors or class of creditors, or of the members of the company or class of members (as the case may be), to be summoned in such manner as the court directs.
@ref s 901C(1) The court may, on an application under this subsection, order a meeting (src:12360)
GIVEN `an application under section 901C(1) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901C(1) the court may order a meeting of the creditors, class of creditors, members or class of members` MEANS
    IF `an application under section 901C(1) has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on an application under this subsection"

-- JURAL the company, any creditor or member: power to apply | the court: liability to hear it
-- src:12361 | (2) An application under subsection (1) may be made by—
-- src:12362 | (a) the company,
-- src:12363 | (b) any creditor or member of the company,
-- src:12364 | (c) if the company is being wound up, the liquidator, or
-- src:12365 | (d) if the company is in administration, the administrator.
@ref s 901C(2) Who may apply (src:12361-12365)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 896(2) applicant`
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901C(2) the person may apply to the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 896(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is being wound up, the liquidator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F29)
    WHEN `s 896(2) the administrator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is in administration` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is in administration, the administrator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F29)
    WHEN `s 896(2) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list of those who may apply does not say "only"

-- JURAL the creditor or member whose rights are affected: claim to participate | the company and the court: duty to permit it
-- src:12366 | (3) Every creditor or member of the company whose rights are affected by the compromise or arrangement must be permitted to participate in a meeting ordered to be summoned under subsection (1).
@ref s 901C(3) Every creditor or member whose rights are affected must be permitted to participate (src:12366)
GIVEN `a meeting is ordered to be summoned under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a creditor or member of the company whose rights are affected by the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901C(3) the person must be permitted to participate in the meeting` MEANS
    IF `a meeting is ordered to be summoned under subsection (1)` AND `the person is a creditor or member of the company whose rights are affected by the compromise or arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every creditor or member of the company whose rights are affected by the compromise or arrangement must be permitted to participate in a meeting ordered to be summoned under subsection (1)"

-- JURAL the class of creditors or members: immunity from the right in (3) if the court so finds | the creditors and members: disability to insist on participation
-- src:12367 | (4) But subsection (3) does not apply in relation to a class of creditors or members of the company if, on an application under this subsection, the court is satisfied that none of the members of that class has a genuine economic interest in the company.
@ref s 901C(4) Subsection (3) does not apply to a class that has no genuine economic interest in the company (src:12367)
GIVEN `on an application under subsection (4) the court is satisfied that none of the members of that class has a genuine economic interest in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901C(4) subsection (3) does not apply in relation to the class` MEANS
    IF `on an application under subsection (4) the court is satisfied that none of the members of that class has a genuine economic interest in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (3) does not apply in relation to a class of creditors or members of the company if, on an application under this subsection, the court is satisfied" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))

-- src:12368 | (5) An application under subsection (4) is to be made by the person who made the application under subsection (1) in respect of the compromise or arrangement.
@ref s 901C(5) The application under subsection (4) is made by the person who applied under subsection (1) (src:12368)
GIVEN `the person made the application under subsection (1) in respect of the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901C(5) the person is the one who is to make the application under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the person made the application under subsection (1) in respect of the compromise or arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under subsection (4) is to be made by the person who made the application under subsection (1)"

-- src:12369 | (6) Section 323 (representation of corporations at meetings) applies to a meeting of creditors under this section as to a meeting of the company (references to a member of the company being read as references to a creditor).
@ref s 901C(6) Section 323 applies to a meeting of creditors under this section (src:12369)
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting of creditors under section 901C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901C(6) section 323 applies to the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a meeting of creditors under section 901C`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to a meeting of creditors under this section"

-- JURAL none (a signpost whose effect is s 901H)
-- src:12370 | (7) This section is subject to section 901H (moratorium debts, etc).
@ref s 901C(7) This section is subject to section 901H (src:12370)
GIVEN `s 901H(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901C(7) section 901C is subject to section 901H` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901H(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 901H does not apply, and s 901C(7) says nothing else
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 901H applies is not known

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Statement to be circulated or made available (s 897); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Statement to be circulated or made available (s 901D)`

DECLARE `s 901D(1) how a notice summoning the meeting is given` IS ONE OF
    `s 901D(1) sent to a creditor or member`
    `s 901D(1) given by advertisement`

-- JURAL the creditor or member: claim to the statement | the company: duty to send it (s 901D(1)(a))
-- src:12372 | (1) Where a meeting is summoned under section 901C—
-- src:12373 | (a) every notice summoning the meeting that is sent to a creditor or member must be accompanied by a statement complying with this section, and
-- src:12374 | (b) every notice summoning the meeting that is given by advertisement must either—
-- src:12375 | (i) include such a statement, or
-- src:12376 | (ii) state where and how creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting may obtain copies of such a statement.
@ref s 901D(1) The notice must be accompanied by, or give access to, a statement (src:12372-12376)
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 901C` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `s 901D(1) how a notice summoning the meeting is given`
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement complying with section 901D` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advertisement includes such a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advertisement states where and how creditors or members entitled to attend may obtain copies of such a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901D(1) the notice summoning the meeting satisfies the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a meeting is summoned under section 901C`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a meeting is summoned under section 901C" (the requirement does not arise)
    ELSE CONSIDER how
         WHEN `s 901D(1) sent to a creditor or member` THEN
             IF `the notice is accompanied by a statement complying with section 901D`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by a statement complying with this section" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)
         WHEN `s 901D(1) given by advertisement` THEN
             IF `the advertisement includes such a statement` OR `the advertisement states where and how creditors or members entitled to attend may obtain copies of such a statement`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must either— (i) include such a statement, or (ii) state where and how"

-- JURAL the company: duty to explain | the creditors and members: claim to the explanation (s 901D(2)); interests of directors: duty of disclosure | the company (s 901D(2)(b))
-- src:12377 | (2) The statement must—
-- src:12378 | (a) explain the effect of the compromise or arrangement, and
-- src:12379 | (b) in particular, state—
-- src:12380 | (i) any material interests of the directors of the company (whether as directors or as members or as creditors of the company or otherwise), and
-- src:12381 | (ii) the effect on those interests of the compromise or arrangement, in so far as it is different from the effect on the like interests of other persons.
@ref s 901D(2) What the statement must explain and state (src:12377-12381)
GIVEN `the statement explains the effect of the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states any material interests of the directors of the company (whether as directors or as members or as creditors of the company or otherwise)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states the effect on those interests of the compromise or arrangement, in so far as it is different from the effect on the like interests of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901D(2) the statement complies` MEANS
    IF `the statement explains the effect of the compromise or arrangement`
       AND `the statement states any material interests of the directors of the company (whether as directors or as members or as creditors of the company or otherwise)`
       AND `the statement states the effect on those interests of the compromise or arrangement, in so far as it is different from the effect on the like interests of other persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement must— (a) explain the effect of the compromise or arrangement, and (b) in particular, state"

-- src:12382 | (3) Where the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders of the company, the statement must give the like explanation as respects the trustees of any deed for securing the issue of the debentures as it is required to give as respects the company’s directors.
@ref s 901D(3) Debenture holders: the like explanation as respects the trustees (src:12382)
GIVEN `the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the like explanation as respects the trustees of any deed for securing the issue of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901D(3) the statement complies as respects debenture holders` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders" (the text requires nothing here otherwise)
    ELSE IF `the statement gives the like explanation as respects the trustees of any deed for securing the issue of the debentures`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the statement must give the like explanation as respects the trustees"

-- JURAL the creditor or member entitled to attend: claim to a free copy | the company: duty to provide it
-- src:12383 | (4) Where a notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting, every such creditor or member is entitled, on making application in the manner indicated by the notice, to be provided by the company with a copy of the statement free of charge.
@ref s 901D(4) A creditor or member may have a copy of the statement free of charge (src:12383)
GIVEN `the notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied in the manner indicated by the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901D(4) the person is entitled to be provided by the company with a copy of the statement free of charge` MEANS
    IF `the notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting`
       AND `the person is a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting`
       AND `the person has applied in the manner indicated by the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a notice given by advertisement states ... every such creditor or member is entitled, on making application in the manner indicated by the notice"

-- The offence of default: the company, and every officer of the company who is in default, subject to subsection (7).
-- JURAL the State (a prosecuting power) | the company and every officer in default: liability to conviction
-- src:12384 | (5) If a company makes default in complying with any requirement of this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:12385 | (a) the company, and
-- src:12386 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:12387 | This is subject to subsection (7).
-- src:12388 | (6) For this purpose the following are treated as officers of the company—
-- src:12389 | (a) a liquidator or administrator of the company, and
-- src:12390 | (b) a trustee of a deed for securing the issue of debentures of the company.
-- src:12391 | (7) A person is not guilty of an offence under this section if the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of the director’s or (as the case may be) the trustee’s interests.
@ref s 901D(5)-(7) Offence by the company and every officer in default; who counts as an officer; the defence (src:12384-12391)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with any requirement of section 901D` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 897(5) person charged with the default`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of the director's or (as the case may be) the trustee's interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901D(5) the person is guilty of an offence under section 901D` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the company makes default in complying with any requirement of section 901D`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with any requirement of this section, an offence is committed by"
        IF `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of the director's or (as the case may be) the trustee's interests`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not guilty of an offence under this section if the person shows that the default was due to the refusal"
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) any other person`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the offence is committed by "(a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default": no one else is named
        OTHERWISE `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- an officer, a liquidator or administrator, or a trustee (subsection (6) treats them as officers): guilty only if in default; JUST FALSE is the "who is in default" no, supplied by s 1121

-- A defence the person must show (the 2026-11-05 ruling (b)): when it is not shown, the answer is that THIS provision gives no defence on these facts.
@ref s 901D(7) The defence: refusal of a director or trustee to supply particulars (src:12391)
GIVEN `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of the director's or (as the case may be) the trustee's interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901D(7) section 901D(7) gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of the director's or (as the case may be) the trustee's interests`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person shows that the default was due to the refusal" (this section gives no defence on these facts, not "no defence at all")

-- The penalty is split by country (the difference from s 897(8)): England and Wales, a fine; Scotland or Northern Ireland, a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
-- JURAL the State | the person guilty: liability to the penalty
-- src:12392 | (8) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:12393 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:12394 | (b) on summary conviction in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:12395 | (c) on summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 901D(8) The penalty (src:12392-12395)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 901D(8) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode `a fine without a stated limit`) -- "(a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine"
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode `a fine without a stated limit`) -- "(b) on summary conviction in England and Wales, to a fine"
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)) -- "(c) on summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum"
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1))
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty on summary conviction depends on the country and the conviction is not said to be in one of the three places

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Duty of directors and trustees to provide information (s 898); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Duty of directors and trustees to provide information (s 901E)`

-- JURAL the company: claim to notice of a director's or trustee's matters | any director of the company and any trustee for its debenture holders: duty to give it
-- src:12397 | (1) It is the duty of—
-- src:12398 | (a) any director of the company, and
-- src:12399 | (b) any trustee for its debenture holders,
-- src:12400 | to give notice to the company of such matters relating to that director or trustee as may be necessary for the purposes of section 901D (explanatory statement to be circulated or made available).
@ref s 901E(1) The duty of a director or trustee to give the company notice of matters relating to that director or trustee (src:12397-12400)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter relates to that director or trustee and is necessary for the purposes of section 901D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901E(1) the person is under a duty to give the company notice of the matter` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` AND `the matter relates to that director or trustee and is necessary for the purposes of section 901D`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any director of the company, and any trustee for its debenture holders, to give notice to the company of such matters relating to that director or trustee as may be necessary"

-- JURAL the State | any person who makes default in complying with section 901E: liability to conviction (s 901E(2)); the penalty (s 901E(3))
-- src:12401 | (2) Any person who makes default in complying with this section commits an offence.
-- src:12402 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 901E(2)-(3) Offence of default and its penalty (src:12401-12402)
GIVEN `the person makes default in complying with section 901E` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901E(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person makes default in complying with section 901E`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who makes default in complying with this section commits an offence"

GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 901E(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 897(8) the conviction is a summary conviction` mode
    THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale" says nothing of conviction on indictment

§§ `Court sanction for compromise or arrangement (s 901F)`

-- The difference from s 899(1): no headcount test. "a number representing 75% in value" and no "majority in number" (fork F5).
-- JURAL the company, any creditor or member: power to apply | the court: power to sanction | those bound: liability
-- src:12405 | (1) If a number representing 75% in value of the creditors or class of creditors or members or class of members (as the case may be), present and voting either in person or by proxy at the meeting summoned under section 901C, agree a compromise or arrangement, the court may, on an application under this section, sanction the compromise or arrangement.
@ref s 901F(1) If a number representing 75% in value agree, the court may sanction (src:12405)
GIVEN `an application under section 901F has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value represented by those present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 901C` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those who agree the compromise or arrangement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901F(1) the court may sanction the compromise or arrangement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an application under section 901F has been made`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, on an application under this section, sanction"
        IF `the value represented by those who agree the compromise or arrangement` AT LEAST (0.75 TIMES `the value represented by those present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 901C`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a number representing 75% in value of the creditors or class of creditors or members or class of members ... agree a compromise or arrangement, the court may" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F30)

-- JURAL none (a signpost whose effect is ss 901G and 901H)
-- src:12406 | (2) Subsection (1) is subject to—
-- src:12407 | (a) section 901G (sanction for compromise or arrangement where one or more classes dissent), and
-- src:12408 | (b) section 901H (moratorium debts, etc).
@ref s 901F(2) Subsection (1) is subject to sections 901G and 901H (src:12406-12408)
GIVEN `s 901G(2) the dissent of the dissenting class does not prevent the court from sanctioning under section 901F` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 901H(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901F(2) section 901F(1) is subject to sections 901G and 901H` MEANS
    IF `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 901G(2) the dissent of the dissenting class does not prevent the court from sanctioning under section 901F`, `s 901H(1) this section applies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither section 901G nor section 901H is engaged, and s 901F(2) says nothing else

-- JURAL the company, any creditor or member: power to apply | the court: liability to hear it
-- src:12409 | (3) An application under this section may be made by—
-- src:12410 | (a) the company,
-- src:12411 | (b) any creditor or member of the company,
-- src:12412 | (c) if the company is being wound up, the liquidator, or
-- src:12413 | (d) if the company is in administration, the administrator.
@ref s 901F(3) Who may apply (src:12409-12413)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 896(2) applicant`
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901F(3) the person may apply to the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 896(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is being wound up, the liquidator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F31)
    WHEN `s 896(2) the administrator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is in administration` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is in administration, the administrator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F31)
    WHEN `s 896(2) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list of those who may apply does not say "only"

DECLARE `s 901F(4) provision the court may make by the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 901F(4)(a) provide for the appointment of the administrator or liquidator to cease to have effect`
    `s 901F(4)(b) stay or sist all proceedings in the administration or the winding up`
    `s 901F(4)(c) impose requirements with respect to the conduct of the administration or the winding up which the court thinks appropriate`
    `s 901F(4) any other provision`

-- JURAL the court: power over the administration or winding up | the administrator or liquidator: liability to its terms
-- src:12414 | (4) Where the court makes an order under this section in relation to a company that is in administration or is being wound up, the court may by the order—
-- src:12415 | (a) provide for the appointment of the administrator or liquidator to cease to have effect;
-- src:12416 | (b) stay or sist all proceedings in the administration or the winding up;
-- src:12417 | (c) impose any requirements with respect to the conduct of the administration or the winding up which the court thinks appropriate for facilitating the compromise or arrangement.
@ref s 901F(4) Where the company is in administration or being wound up, the court may by the order make provision about the administration or winding up (src:12414-12417)
GIVEN `the company is in administration or is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A `s 901F(4) provision the court may make by the order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901F(4) the court may by the order make the provision` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is in administration or is being wound up`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the court makes an order under this section in relation to a company that is in administration or is being wound up"
    ELSE CONSIDER provision
         WHEN `s 901F(4) any other provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the court may by the order" lists, and does not say "only"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- JURAL the company, the creditors or class, the members or class, the liquidator and contributories: liability to be bound
-- src:12418 | (5) A compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court is binding—
-- src:12419 | (a) on all creditors or the class of creditors or on the members or class of members (as the case may be), and
-- src:12420 | (b) on the company or, in the case of a company in the course of being wound up, the liquidator and contributories of the company.
@ref s 901F(5) A sanctioned compromise or arrangement is binding (src:12418-12420)
GIVEN `the court has sanctioned the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 899(3) person said to be bound`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901F(5) the compromise or arrangement is binding on the person` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the court has sanctioned the compromise or arrangement`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court is binding"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 899(3) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "is binding" names the creditors, members, the company, the liquidator and contributories, and does not say "only"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The "until" bar (2026-11-05 ruling (d)). The step that lifts the bar depends on the company: an overseas company that is not required
-- to register particulars under s 1046 (a seam: coa23) must have the copy published in the Gazette; any other company, delivered to the registrar.
-- JURAL the registrar or the Gazette (receipt) | the company: duty to deliver or publish; those the order affects: no right to rely on it before
-- src:12421 | (6) The court’s order has no effect until a copy of it has been—
-- src:12422 | (a) in the case of an overseas company that is not required to register particulars under section 1046, published in the Gazette, or
-- src:12423 | (b) in any other case, delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 901F(6) The court's order has no effect until a copy is published in the Gazette or delivered to the registrar (src:12421-12423)
GIVEN `the company is an overseas company that is not required to register particulars under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the order has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the order has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901F(6) the court's order cannot yet have effect` MEANS
    IF `the company is an overseas company that is not required to register particulars under section 1046`
    THEN (IF `a copy of the order has been published in the Gazette`
          THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has no effect until a copy of it has been— (a) in the case of an overseas company ..., published in the Gazette" (the bar has lifted)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE (IF `a copy of the order has been delivered to the registrar`
          THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in any other case, delivered to the registrar" (the bar has lifted)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§§ `Sanction for compromise or arrangement where one or more classes dissent (s 901G)`

-- The 75% test is in value only. denominators: "present and voting", so a class of value 0 present and voting is not covered.
-- JURAL none (a rule fixing when the section applies)
-- src:12425 | (1) This section applies if the compromise or arrangement is not agreed by a number representing at least 75% in value of a class of creditors or (as the case may be) of members of the company (“the dissenting class”), present and voting either in person or by proxy at the meeting summoned under section 901C.
@ref s 901G(1) The section applies if a class does not agree by 75% in value (src:12425)
GIVEN `the value represented by the members of the class present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 901C` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those of them who agree the compromise or arrangement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901G(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the value represented by the members of the class present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 901C` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no value present and voting in the class, so no percentage can be taken
    ELSE IF `the value represented by those of them who agree the compromise or arrangement` LESS THAN (0.75 TIMES `the value represented by the members of the class present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 901C`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if the compromise or arrangement is not agreed by a number representing at least 75% in value of a class" (the class agreed by at least 75%)

-- JURAL the dissenting class: immunity from being outvoted only if conditions A and B are not met | the court: power to sanction despite the dissent
-- src:12426 | (2) If conditions A and B are met, the fact that the dissenting class has not agreed the compromise or arrangement does not prevent the court from sanctioning it under section 901F.
@ref s 901G(2) If conditions A and B are met, the dissent of a class does not prevent the court sanctioning (src:12426)
GIVEN `s 901G(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 901G(3) condition A is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 901G(5) condition B is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901G(2) the dissent of the dissenting class does not prevent the court from sanctioning under section 901F` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901G(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies if the compromise or arrangement is not agreed by" a class; where every class agreed there is no dissent to speak of
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `s 901G(3) condition A is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 901G(5) condition B is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If conditions A and B are met, the fact that the dissenting class has not agreed ... does not prevent the court" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
            IF `s 901G(3) condition A is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 901G(5) condition B is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known and neither condition has failed

-- The court's satisfaction is the judgment the text hands to the court: a conditional input (fork F4).
-- src:12427 | (3) Condition A is that the court is satisfied that, if the compromise or arrangement were to be sanctioned under section 901F, none of the members of the dissenting class would be any worse off than they would be in the event of the relevant alternative (see subsection (4)).
@ref s 901G(3) Condition A: none of the dissenting class would be any worse off than in the relevant alternative (src:12427)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that, if the compromise or arrangement were sanctioned under section 901F, none of the members of the dissenting class would be any worse off than they would be in the event of the relevant alternative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901G(3) condition A is met` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that, if the compromise or arrangement were sanctioned under section 901F, none of the members of the dissenting class would be any worse off than they would be in the event of the relevant alternative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition A is that the court is satisfied that, if the compromise or arrangement were to be sanctioned under section 901F, none of the members of the dissenting class would be any worse off"

-- "whatever the court considers would be most likely to occur": the answer is the court's own view, supplied as a text (NOTHING = not known).
-- src:12428 | (4) For the purposes of this section “the relevant alternative” is whatever the court considers would be most likely to occur in relation to the company if the compromise or arrangement were not sanctioned under section 901F.
@ref s 901G(4) The relevant alternative is whatever the court considers most likely to occur if the compromise or arrangement were not sanctioned (src:12428)
GIVEN `what the court considers would be most likely to occur in relation to the company if the compromise or arrangement were not sanctioned under section 901F` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 901G(4) the relevant alternative` MEANS
    `what the court considers would be most likely to occur in relation to the company if the compromise or arrangement were not sanctioned under section 901F` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the court's view is its own and is not in the sources; "means" gives no other source

-- Condition B: "a number representing 75% in value of a class ... present and voting ... who would receive a payment, or have a genuine
-- economic interest in the company, in the event of the relevant alternative".
-- src:12429 | (5) Condition B is that the compromise or arrangement has been agreed by a number representing 75% in value of a class of creditors or (as the case may be) of members, present and voting either in person or by proxy at the meeting summoned under section 901C, who would receive a payment, or have a genuine economic interest in the company, in the event of the relevant alternative.
@ref s 901G(5) Condition B: agreed by 75% in value of a class who would receive a payment or have a genuine economic interest in the relevant alternative (src:12429)
GIVEN `the value represented by the members of a class present and voting who would receive a payment, or have a genuine economic interest in the company, in the event of the relevant alternative` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those of them who agree the compromise or arrangement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901G(5) condition B is met` MEANS
    IF `the value represented by the members of a class present and voting who would receive a payment, or have a genuine economic interest in the company, in the event of the relevant alternative` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no value in such a class, so no percentage can be taken
    ELSE IF `the value represented by those of them who agree the compromise or arrangement` AT LEAST (0.75 TIMES `the value represented by the members of a class present and voting who would receive a payment, or have a genuine economic interest in the company, in the event of the relevant alternative`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition B is that the compromise or arrangement has been agreed by a number representing 75% in value of a class"

-- src:12430 | (6) The Secretary of State may by regulations amend this section for the purpose of—
-- src:12431 | (a) adding to the conditions that must be met for the purposes of this section;
-- src:12432 | (b) removing or varying any of those conditions.
-- src:12433 | (7) Regulations under subsection (6) are subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
-- s 901G(6)-(7): the Secretary of State's power to amend this section by regulations, and the affirmative procedure: machinery (inert, reason 2). No L4.

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Moratorium debts, etc (s 899A); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Moratorium debts, etc (s 901H)`

-- Period: "the period of 12 weeks beginning with the day after the end of any moratorium": the 84 days from the day after the
-- moratorium ended; an application "before the end of the period" is made on or before the last of those days (fork F4).
-- JURAL none (a rule fixing when the section applies)
-- src:12436 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:12437 | (a) an application under section 901C(1) in respect of a compromise or arrangement is made before the end of the period of 12 weeks beginning with the day after the end of any moratorium for the company under Part A1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 1A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)), and
-- src:12438 | (b) the creditors with whom the compromise or arrangement is proposed include any relevant creditors (see subsection (2)).
@ref s 901H(1) This section applies where an application is made within 12 weeks of the end of a moratorium and relevant creditors are included (src:12436-12438)
GIVEN `date of the application under section 901C(1)` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the moratorium under Part A1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 1A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A DATE
      `the creditors with whom the compromise or arrangement is proposed include any relevant creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901H(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `date of the application under section 901C(1)` AT MOST (`the last day of the moratorium under Part A1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 1A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` PLUS 84)
       AND `the creditors with whom the compromise or arrangement is proposed include any relevant creditors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (an application after the 12 weeks, or no relevant creditor)

-- src:12439 | (2) In this section “relevant creditor” means—
-- src:12440 | (a) a creditor in respect of a moratorium debt, or
-- src:12441 | (b) a creditor in respect of a priority pre-moratorium debt.
@ref s 901H(2) "relevant creditor" (src:12439-12441)
GIVEN `the creditor is a creditor in respect of a moratorium debt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor is a creditor in respect of a priority pre-moratorium debt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901H(2) the creditor is a relevant creditor` MEANS
    IF `the creditor is a creditor in respect of a moratorium debt` OR `the creditor is a creditor in respect of a priority pre-moratorium debt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant creditor” means"

-- JURAL the relevant creditor: disability (it may not participate) | the meeting
-- src:12442 | (3) The relevant creditors may not participate in the meeting summoned under section 901C.
@ref s 901H(3) Relevant creditors may not participate in the meeting (src:12442)
GIVEN `s 901H(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the creditor is a relevant creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901H(3) the relevant creditor may participate in the meeting summoned under section 901C` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901H(1) this section applies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether this section applies is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is in a section that applies only "where" its conditions are met
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the creditor is a relevant creditor`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant creditors may not participate in the meeting summoned under section 901C"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a creditor who is not a relevant creditor is not mentioned

-- JURAL the relevant creditor: claim to a statement | the company: duty to send it (s 901H(4)(a))
-- src:12443 | (4) For the purposes of section 901D (statement to be circulated or made available)—
-- src:12444 | (a) the requirement in section 901D(1)(a) is to be read as including a requirement to send each relevant creditor a statement complying with section 901D;
-- src:12445 | (b) any reference to creditors entitled to attend the meeting summoned under section 901C includes a reference to relevant creditors.
@ref s 901H(4) Section 897 applies to relevant creditors (src:12443-12445)
GIVEN `s 901H(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the creditor is a relevant creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901H(4) the relevant creditor is within section 901D as a creditor entitled to be sent the statement and to attend` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901H(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the creditor is a relevant creditor`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a creditor who is not a relevant creditor is not mentioned
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of section 901D" in a section that applies only "where" its conditions are met
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether this section applies is not known

-- JURAL the creditor (a relevant creditor that has not agreed): immunity from provision in the arrangement | the court: disability to sanction
-- src:12446 | (5) The court may not sanction the compromise or arrangement under section 901F if it includes provision in respect of any relevant creditor who has not agreed to it.
@ref s 901H(5) The court may not sanction an arrangement that includes provision for a relevant creditor who has not agreed (src:12446)
GIVEN `s 901H(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the compromise or arrangement includes provision in respect of a relevant creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that relevant creditor has agreed to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901H(5) the court may sanction the compromise or arrangement under section 901F` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901H(1) this section applies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether this section applies is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is in a section that applies only "where" its conditions are met
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the compromise or arrangement includes provision in respect of a relevant creditor` AND NOT (`that relevant creditor has agreed to it`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court may not sanction the compromise or arrangement under section 901F if it includes provision in respect of any relevant creditor who has not agreed to it"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar names only a relevant creditor who has not agreed

DECLARE `s 901H(6) kind of moratorium` IS ONE OF
    `s 901H(6) a moratorium under Part A1 of the Insolvency Act 1986`
    `s 901H(6) a moratorium under Part 1A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`

-- "moratorium debt" and "priority pre-moratorium debt" have the same meaning as in s 174A of the 1986 Act / Article 148A of the 1989 Order,
-- which are not among the sources: the borrowed answer is an input (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE as that provision says; NOTHING = not known).
-- src:12447 | (6) In this section—
-- src:12448 | “moratorium debt”—
-- src:12449 | (a) in the case of a moratorium under Part A1 of the Insolvency Act 1986, has the same meaning as in section 174A of that Act;
-- src:12450 | (b) in the case of a moratorium under Part 1A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989, has the same meaning as in Article 148A of that Order;
-- src:12451 | “priority pre-moratorium debt”—
-- src:12452 | (a) in the case of a moratorium under Part A1 of the Insolvency Act 1986, has the same meaning as in section 174A of that Act;
-- src:12453 | (b) in the case of a moratorium under Part 1A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989, has the same meaning as in Article 148A of that Order.
@ref s 901H(6) "moratorium debt" and "priority pre-moratorium debt" have the meaning in the Insolvency Act 1986 or the 1989 Order (src:12447-12453)
GIVEN moratorium IS A `s 901H(6) kind of moratorium`
      `the debt has the meaning given by section 174A of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 148A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 as the case may be, for a moratorium debt or a priority pre-moratorium debt` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901H(6) the debt is a moratorium debt or a priority pre-moratorium debt` MEANS
    CONSIDER moratorium
    WHEN `s 901H(6) a moratorium under Part A1 of the Insolvency Act 1986` THEN `the debt has the meaning given by section 174A of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 148A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 as the case may be, for a moratorium debt or a priority pre-moratorium debt` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 174A of that Act is not among the sources
    WHEN `s 901H(6) a moratorium under Part 1A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` THEN `the debt has the meaning given by section 174A of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 148A of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 as the case may be, for a moratorium debt or a priority pre-moratorium debt` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 148A of that Order is not among the sources

§§ `Pension schemes (s 901I)`

-- JURAL the Pensions Regulator: claim to a copy of every notice or document sent to a creditor | the company: duty to send it
-- src:12455 | (1) In a case where the company in respect of which a compromise or arrangement is proposed is or has been an employer in respect of an occupational pension scheme that is not a money purchase scheme, any notice or other document required to be sent to a creditor of the company must also be sent to the Pensions Regulator.
@ref s 901I(1) Notices to creditors must also be sent to the Pensions Regulator (src:12455)
GIVEN `the company is or has been an employer in respect of an occupational pension scheme that is not a money purchase scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice or other document is required to be sent to a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice or other document has also been sent to the Pensions Regulator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901I(1) the notice or other document has been sent to the Pensions Regulator as the section requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is or has been an employer in respect of an occupational pension scheme that is not a money purchase scheme` AND `the notice or other document is required to be sent to a creditor of the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case where the company ... is or has been an employer in respect of an occupational pension scheme that is not a money purchase scheme, any notice or other document required to be sent to a creditor" (the requirement does not arise)
    ELSE IF `the notice or other document has also been sent to the Pensions Regulator`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must also be sent to the Pensions Regulator" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

