-- (instantiated from the twin block of Powers of court to facilitate reconstruction or amalgamation (s 900); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Powers of court to facilitate reconstruction or amalgamation (s 901J)`

-- JURAL none (a rule fixing when the section applies)
-- src:12483 | (1) This section applies where application is made to the court under section 901F to sanction a compromise or arrangement and it is shown that—
-- src:12484 | (a) the compromise or arrangement is proposed in connection with a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies, and
-- src:12485 | (b) under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme (a “transferor company”) is to be transferred to another company (“the transferee company”).
@ref s 901J(1) The section applies where a scheme of reconstruction or amalgamation involves a transfer (src:12483-12485)
GIVEN `application is made to the court under section 901F to sanction a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compromise or arrangement is proposed in connection with a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme is to be transferred to another company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901J(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `application is made to the court under section 901F to sanction a compromise or arrangement`
       AND `the compromise or arrangement is proposed in connection with a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies`
       AND `under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme is to be transferred to another company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where application is made to the court under section 901F to sanction a compromise or arrangement and it is shown that"

DECLARE `s 901J(2) matter for which the court may make provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 901J(2)(a) the transfer to the transferee company of the undertaking, property or liabilities of a transferor company`
    `s 901J(2)(b) the allotting or appropriation by the transferee company of shares, debentures, policies or other like interests`
    `s 901J(2)(c) the continuation by or against the transferee company of legal proceedings pending by or against a transferor company`
    `s 901J(2)(d) the dissolution, without winding up, of a transferor company`
    `s 901J(2)(e) the provision for persons who dissent from the compromise or arrangement`
    `s 901J(2)(f) incidental, consequential and supplemental matters necessary to secure that the reconstruction or amalgamation is fully and effectively carried out`
    `s 901J(2) any other matter`

-- JURAL the court: power to make the provision | the companies, creditors and members concerned: liability to it
-- src:12486 | (2) The court may, either by the order sanctioning the compromise or arrangement or by a subsequent order, make provision for all or any of the following matters—
-- src:12487 | (a) the transfer to the transferee company of the whole or any part of the undertaking and of the property or liabilities of any transferor company;
-- src:12488 | (b) the allotting or appropriation by the transferee company of any shares, debentures, policies or other like interests in that company which under the compromise or arrangement are to be allotted or appropriated by that company to or for any person;
-- src:12489 | (c) the continuation by or against the transferee company of any legal proceedings pending by or against any transferor company;
-- src:12490 | (d) the dissolution, without winding up, of any transferor company;
-- src:12491 | (e) the provision to be made for any persons who, within such time and in such manner as the court directs, dissent from the compromise or arrangement;
-- src:12492 | (f) such incidental, consequential and supplemental matters as are necessary to secure that the reconstruction or amalgamation is fully and effectively carried out.
@ref s 901J(2) The matters for which the court may make provision (src:12486-12492)
GIVEN `s 901J(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 901J(2) matter for which the court may make provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901J(2) the court may make provision for the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901J(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (the court has the powers of this section only where it applies)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `s 901J(2) any other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "make provision for all or any of the following matters" lists, and does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- JURAL the transferee company: right to the property and the burden of the liabilities | the transferor company: disability (the property passes without further act)
-- src:12493 | (3) If an order under this section provides for the transfer of property or liabilities—
-- src:12494 | (a) the property is by virtue of the order transferred to, and vests in, the transferee company, and
-- src:12495 | (b) the liabilities are, by virtue of the order, transferred to and become liabilities of that company.
@ref s 901J(3) The transfer of property or liabilities takes effect by virtue of the order (src:12493-12495)
GIVEN `an order under section 901J provides for the transfer of property or liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901J(3) the property vests in, and the liabilities become liabilities of, the transferee company by virtue of the order` MEANS
    IF `an order under section 901J provides for the transfer of property or liabilities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order under this section provides for the transfer of property or liabilities" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))

-- src:12496 | (4) The property (if the order so directs) vests freed from any charge that is by virtue of the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect.
@ref s 901J(4) The property vests freed from a charge if the order so directs (src:12496)
GIVEN `the order so directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is by virtue of the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901J(4) the property vests freed from the charge` MEANS
    IF `the order so directs` AND `the charge is by virtue of the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The property (if the order so directs) vests freed from any charge that is by virtue of the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect"

-- src:12497 | (5) In this section—
-- src:12498 | “property” includes property, rights and powers of every description; and
-- src:12499 | “liabilities” includes duties.
@ref s 901J(5) "property" includes property, rights and powers of every description; "liabilities" includes duties (src:12497-12499)
GIVEN `the thing is property, a right or a power of any description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901J(5) the thing is property` MEANS
    IF `the thing is property, a right or a power of any description` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“property” includes property, rights and powers of every description"

GIVEN `the thing is a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901J(5) the thing is a liability` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a duty` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“liabilities” includes duties"

-- "within seven days after its making": the seventh day after the order is made is the last day (day 0 is the day of the order).
-- date of delivery NOTHING means not yet delivered; today is the day the question is asked.
-- JURAL the registrar (receipt) | every company in relation to which an order is made: duty to cause a copy to be delivered within seven days
-- src:12500 | (6) Every company in relation to which an order is made under this section must cause a copy of the order to be delivered to the registrar within seven days after its making.
@ref s 901J(6) The company must cause a copy of the order to be delivered to the registrar within seven days after its making (src:12500)
GIVEN `date the order was made` IS A DATE
      `date a copy was delivered to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
      today IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901J(6) the company delivered a copy of the order to the registrar in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date a copy was delivered to the registrar`
    WHEN JUST delivered THEN
        IF delivered AT LEAST `date the order was made` AND delivered AT MOST (`date the order was made` PLUS 7)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within seven days after its making"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF today AT MOST (`date the order was made` PLUS 7)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the seven days have not run out and no copy has been delivered yet
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within seven days after its making" (no copy was delivered, and the period has ended)

@ref s 901J(6) The duty as a regulative rule (src:12500)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 901J(6) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` Company Registrar "deliver a copy of the order to the registrar"
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "a copy of the order was not delivered to the registrar within seven days after its making (s 901J(6))"

-- The offence: the company, and every officer of the company who is in default (s 901J(7)); no defence in this section.
-- JURAL the State | the company and every officer in default: liability to conviction
-- src:12501 | (7) If default is made in complying with subsection (6) an offence is committed by—
-- src:12502 | (a) the company, and
-- src:12503 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 901J(7) Offence if default is made in complying with subsection (6) (src:12501-12503)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 901J(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 897(5) person charged with the default`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901J(7) the person is guilty of an offence under section 901J(7)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`default is made in complying with section 901J(6)`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (6) an offence is committed by"
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) any other person`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the offence is committed by "(a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
        OTHERWISE `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:12504 | (8) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (7) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 901J(8) The penalty: level 3 and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 3 (src:12504)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 901J(8) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 897(8) the conviction is a summary conviction` mode
    THEN JUST (`s 900(8) a penalty of a fine and a daily default fine for continued contravention` mode (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1) (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is liable on summary conviction to a fine" says nothing of conviction on indictment

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Obligations of company with respect to articles etc (s 901); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Obligations of company with respect to articles etc (s 901K)`

-- JURAL none (a rule fixing when the section applies)
-- src:12507 | (1) This section applies—
-- src:12508 | (a) to any order under section 901F (order sanctioning compromise or arrangement), and
-- src:12509 | (b) to any order under section 901J (order facilitating reconstruction or amalgamation) that alters the company’s constitution.
@ref s 901K(1) The section applies to an order under section 901F and to an order under section 901J that alters the constitution (src:12507-12509)
GIVEN `the order is an order under section 901F` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is an order under section 901J that alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901K(1) this section applies to the order` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order under section 901F` OR `the order is an order under section 901J that alters the company's constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies— (a) to any order under section 901F ..., and (b) to any order under section 901J ... that alters the company's constitution"


-- JURAL anyone to whom the company issues a copy of its articles: claim to a copy of the order | the company: duty to accompany each copy of the articles
-- src:12516 | (3) Every copy of the company’s articles issued by the company after the order is made must be accompanied by a copy of the order, unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment.
@ref s 901K(3) Every copy of the articles issued after the order is made must be accompanied by a copy of the order (src:12516)
GIVEN `s 901K(1) this section applies to the order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the articles is issued by the company after the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the articles is accompanied by a copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901K(3) the copy of the articles is accompanied as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901K(1) this section applies to the order`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies to the order is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is in a section that applies only to the orders it names
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT (`the copy of the articles is issued by the company after the order is made`)
                THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every copy of the company's articles issued by the company after the order is made"
            IF `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment`
                THEN JUST TRUE -- "unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment": the exception is met, so nothing more is required and the copy is as the section requires (an "unless" once met: fork F10)
            IF `the copy of the articles is accompanied by a copy of the order`
                THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by a copy of the order" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

DECLARE `s 901K(4) what an article reference means` IS ONE OF
    `s 901K(4)(a) a reference to the effect of the order`
    `s 901K(4)(b) a reference to the articles of a company not having articles`

-- Rules of reading (s 901K(4)): the second argument is what the reference points at.
-- src:12517 | (4) In this section—
-- src:12518 | (a) references to the effect of the order include the effect of the compromise or arrangement to which the order relates, and
-- src:12519 | (b) in the case of a company not having articles, references to its articles are to be read as references to the instrument constituting the company or defining its constitution.
@ref s 901K(4) References to the effect of the order, and to the articles of a company not having articles (src:12517-12519)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 901K(4) what an article reference means`
      `the thing is the effect of the compromise or arrangement to which the order relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is the instrument constituting the company or defining its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901K(4) the thing is within the reference` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 901K(4)(a) a reference to the effect of the order` THEN
        IF `the thing is the effect of the compromise or arrangement to which the order relates` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to the effect of the order include the effect of the compromise or arrangement"
    WHEN `s 901K(4)(b) a reference to the articles of a company not having articles` THEN
        IF `the thing is the instrument constituting the company or defining its constitution` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a company not having articles, references to its articles shall be read as references to the instrument constituting the company or defining its constitution"

-- JURAL the State | the company and every officer in default: liability to conviction (s 901K(5)); the penalty (s 901K(6))
-- src:12520 | (5) If a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:12521 | (a) the company, and
-- src:12522 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 901K(5) Offence if a company makes default in complying with the section (src:12520-12522)
GIVEN `a company makes default in complying with section 901K` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 897(5) person charged with the default`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901K(5) the person is guilty of an offence under section 901K` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a company makes default in complying with section 901K`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by"
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) any other person`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the offence is committed by "(a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
        OTHERWISE `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:12523 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 901K(6) The penalty: level 3 on the standard scale (src:12523)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 901K(6) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 897(8) the conviction is a summary conviction` mode
    THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is liable on summary conviction to a fine" says nothing of conviction on indictment

-- The difference from s 901(2): the copy must be delivered "under section 901F(6)(b) or section 901J(6)" (a second condition).
-- JURAL the registrar (receipt) | the company: duty to accompany the copy of the order with the amended articles, resolution or agreement
-- src:12510 | (2) If—
-- src:12511 | (a) the order amends—
-- src:12512 | (i) the company’s articles, or
-- src:12513 | (ii) any resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies (resolution or agreement affecting a company’s constitution), and
-- src:12514 | (b) a copy of the order is required to be delivered to the registrar by the company under section 901F(6)(b) or section 901J(6),
-- src:12515 | the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the company’s articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended.
@ref s 901K(2) The copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by the amended articles, resolution or agreement (src:12510-12515)
GIVEN `s 901K(1) this section applies to the order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order amends the company's articles or a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the order is required to be delivered to the registrar by the company under section 901F(6)(b) or section 901J(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy delivered to the registrar is accompanied by a copy of the articles, or the resolution or agreement, as amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901K(2) the copy of the order is accompanied as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901K(1) this section applies to the order`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies to the order is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is in a section that applies only to the orders it names
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT (`the order amends the company's articles or a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies` AND `a copy of the order is required to be delivered to the registrar by the company under section 901F(6)(b) or section 901J(6)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If— (a) the order amends ... and (b) a copy of the order is required to be delivered to the registrar by the company under section 901F(6)(b) or section 901J(6)"
        ELSE IF `the copy delivered to the registrar is accompanied by a copy of the articles, or the resolution or agreement, as amended`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

§§ `Power to amend Act (s 901L)`

-- src:12525 | 901L Power to amend Act
-- src:12526 | (1) The Secretary of State may by regulations make any amendment of this Act which the Secretary of State considers necessary or expedient for the purposes of, in consequence of, or for giving full effect to this Part.
-- src:12527 | (2) Regulations under this section are subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
-- s 901L: the Secretary of State's power to amend the Act for the purposes of Part 26A and the affirmative procedure: machinery (inert, reason 2). No L4.

